      "type": "conceptual",
      "split": "confirmation",
      "question": "What specific consequences can an individual face if a company determines they have violated its insider trading policy, even if no legal charges are filed?",
      "quote": "If the Company has a reasonable basis to conclude that you have failed to comply with this Policy, you may be subject to disciplinary action by the Company, up to and including dismissal for cause, regardless of whether or not your failure to comply with this Policy results in a violation of law. It is not necessary for the Company to wait for the filing or conclusion of any civil or criminal action against an alleged violator before taking disciplinary action.",
